******************** - Start of Change History - *******************************; Copyright nineteen eighty seven too nineteen eighty eight.; All rights reserved. Apple Computer, Inc. '87-'88/'88.; 10/21/87; VER .91P; Fixed problem with not being able to have multiple phrases.; 10/21; fixed some problems with returning errors.  WrongTypeErr is not returned; any more.; 10/22/87; Phd and tcd in SeqShutDown, hoping it will fix my bug of not being able to; startup and shut down and play a sequence multiple times.; changed order of start sound call in seqappst call.; Not changing callers pointer in setinst anymore.; Instnum now adds two to offset into inst table instead.; this did    fix the problem of multiple setinsttable calls.; 10/22/87; ver .92P; 10/28/87; Fixed the problem with the Regesters, by aligning the regester info to; the right.; ver .93P; 11/4/87; Changed ppatt and chkoff so that if tick count and duration are equal; the note will be turned off and the delay will not continue.;; The Timing was off by one tick too many. No it's not.; ver .94P; 11/16; If increment is zero sequencer doesn't continue parsing but synthesizer does.; 11/19; Fixed bug dealing with if when tick count wraps.; put in tables for midi.; ver .95P; 11/19; LSB now sets mode 0 = interupts 1 = step mode; MSB of mode sets midi. 1 = midi use enabled.; 12/3; MSB of Duration means that the note is awaiting a NoteOff, is not being used,; or has wrapped around. If it has wraped around the MSB of Track won't be set.; Other wize it will be set.; The high bit of the channel paramater acts the same as the track paramter in; the above note.; the high byte of track in set track sets the channel, if to be used w midi.; supports full midi use. (I think).; ver .96P; 12/7; settrkinfo sets up the midi scratch regester in the trkinfo table, to; determine if midi is on or off.; all midi info should be working correctly now.  Check off and just midi.; ver .97P; 12/8; midi only control command structure has been set up.; 12/9; put in midi3bytes, midi2bytes, midi1byte routines.; 12/14; program change and pitch bend have had midi capability added to them.; 1/4; fixed wrap bug, if tickcount wraps.; 1/5; put in AllNotesOff and FlushBuffer stuff.; ver .98P; 1/12; SeqStartUp now shuts SoundTools if an error occured on NoteSynthStartUp.; 1/12-1/13; changed error chking to match .99P documentation with the exception of:; NoMIDIErr which I dont use, instead I return miNoBufErr.; check if sequencer is active before shutdown and startup.; put in copyright notice.; make compatiable with new MIDI Tool set.; added caller error vector error handling for errors in sequence.; I dont check to see if the sequencer is started or not.; ver .99P; 1-25-88; _SeqStartUP now returns startederr if it's already been started up.; _SeqShutDown now returns nostarterr if it hasn't been started yet.; _StartSeq now returns nostarterr if it hasn't been started yet.; 1-27; fixed bug in user error handler routine. did a pei instead of pea.; 1-28; fixed bug where error handler wasnt being stored on dp.; 1-29; error handler really should have had pei not pea in 1-27.; interupts are disabled when I call the err handling routine.; ver 1.00P; 2-2; I also preserve my databank and directpage when calling the users; error handler and completion routine.; I also supply the user with the databank they had when they made the; _SeqStartUp call. This databank is returned to the Completion routine,; and to the error handling routine.; 2-3; I dont disable all interupts before I call the error handler routine.; I do disable the note synth interupts though for both the error; handling routine and the completion routine.; 2-3; Fixed bug. It wasnt working if you werent using midi.  No it does.; 2-4; Fixed a partial bug in justmidi routine, that was messing up the stack when; I only wanted to do midi.  Its not completly fixed yet though.; 2-5; Check off wasnt building the midi note off corectly when doing only midi.; This should completely fix the bug mentioned in 2-4.; 2-6; Now passes the N.Seq. error to the error handler properly.; fixed stack problem when returning from error handler.; 2-7; Realtime now goes out in real time.; midionebyterawdata is changed to be a system common command.; miditwobytesRawData to be changed to a Hndl to a midi array.; 2-9; There are now Two commands that need to be maed to do a system exclusive; midi command. This is necessary inorder to pass the ptr to the array.; MidiOneByteRawData and MidiTwoByteRawData have been deleted.; I do support a MidiSystemRealTime command now. See documentation for; more specifics on how to make the call.; 3-1; fixed bug where start seq messed up the stack if there was an error.; 3-2; fixed bug in StopSeq if Midi set in Mode.; 3-3; fixed bug in turning off all of the notes.  I am now turning them off; correctly in completion routine, and _SeqAllNotesOff.; 3-7; Seq reset is turning notes off correctly now.; No stack checking on Error Handler; IgnoreInts is set true in stopints and is only set in playseq.; 3-16; Don't turn off and on N.Synth osc any more.; Turn off notes with duration before quiting.; 4-4-88; Fixed problem where sequence is finished before the end of the SeqStart call.; 4-11-88; Fixed bug where I get MIDI's DP in StartSeq not SeqStartUP.; 4-12-88; Vib depth command now gets midi/internal info from reserved paramater.; Interupts disabled in start and stop timer.; 5-2-88; set doneflag to FFFF at startup.; TickWrap doesn't hit a brk any more. ; 5-25-88; Error code wasn't getting returned correctly. It is now fixed.; 5-31-88; Changed sei, cli in instn2ptr to php, sei, plp.; 6-1-88; fixed all of bug, was pei 9 not pea 9.; Now polls MIDI completly.; returns error $1a07 if NSynth is the wrong version needs 1.2P or later.; Can't do a midi flush event.; 10-6-88; Added _StartSeqRel call, this uses the same code as _startseq.  There was also; a change to playseq to add RelAddr which is the relative address to be; added to each pointer to a phrase or pattern, except the first phrase.  ; RelAddr is a new location on my first direct page.********************* - End of Change History - *******************************